                <pb facs="0207" n="103" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg103"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/3702: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai (Cunningham) to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-01-29T20:00:00+08:00">January 29, 1932—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 29—11:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Paragraph 3 of my January 29, 4 p.m. After communicating Japanese Admiral’s
                    message to the Mayor at 6:30 this afternoon at the Japanese Consul[ate] General
                    an armistice was arranged to become effective at 8 o’clock tonight. We await
                    developments.</p>
                <p>Repeated to [Legation?].</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
